jei.immersivenuclear.filter_press.info=3x3x9 multiblock (56 blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Slurry (or neutralized sludge: water and neutralization cake) goes in at the front, on the pump end; the crude solution (or the water) comes out at the front, on the other end; the residue comes out at the side, where the conveyor ends; energy on the heavy engineering blocks. At the back: filter input and spent filter output, to automate the swap. Needs all 28 filters. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
jei.immersivenuclear.filter.info=Filter of the Filtration Unit: the machine takes 28, one per plate. Every batch wears each filter by 1; a spent filter no longer filters and has to be replaced (in the interface or through the ports at the back).
jei.immersivenuclear.processing_reagent.info=Used by the Chemical Processing Unit, 16 per batch, with 16 uranium powder and 8000 mB of water.
jei.immersivenuclear.wet_mineral_residue.info=Solid residue of the Filtration Unit: the cake left between the plates, which falls when they open. Still soaked in the acid leach and radioactive: neutralize it with quicklime (4 residue + 1 quicklime) before using it.
jei.immersivenuclear.neutralized_residue.info=Wet Mineral Residue neutralized with quicklime. Crush it in the IE Crusher for sand and a chance of iron, clay and the little uranium the leaching left behind, or press 4 into an Impure Agglomerate.
jei.immersivenuclear.metal_extractor.info=4x4x4 multiblock (44 blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Chemical effluent in on the left end, depleted effluent out on the right end, the Mixed Metal Deposit out at the back; energy on the heavy engineering blocks of the right end. Each batch: 12000 mB of effluent, prepared, plated out on six plates (256 IF/t for a minute), drained and scraped into 6 deposits; the plates are cleaned while the vat drains. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
jei.immersivenuclear.metal_extractor.plates=Recovery: %s s at %s IF/t, the metals plating out on the six plates
jei.immersivenuclear.mixed_metal_deposit.info=Metal scraped off the Metal Extractor's plates, one per 2000 mB of chemical effluent. Crush it in the IE Crusher: slag, and a chance of iron, aluminium, copper, lead, nickel and uranium nuggets and clay.
jei.immersivenuclear.depleted_effluent.info=What is left of the chemical effluent after the Metal Extractor. Still acidic: send it back to the Chemical Processing Unit (its recycled liquor tank), or neutralize it with quicklime in the IE Mixer (neutralized sludge).
jei.immersivenuclear.uranium_slurry.info=Product of the Chemical Processing Unit; goes into the Filtration Unit.
jei.immersivenuclear.crude_uranium_solution.info=Product of the Filtration Unit: the uranium still dissolved with impurities. Goes on to the chemical separation (next machine).
